+        // Build scripts and their dependencies are always compiled by the stage0
+        // compiler (see `src/bootstrap/src/bin/rustc.rs`), and Cargo's default
+        // build-override compiles them at `-Copt-level=0`. `library/Cargo.toml`
+        // sets `-Cembed-bitcode=yes` for the whole `dist` profile, and Cargo
+        // applies profile rustflags to host units too, so those host units end up
+        // asking for a ThinLTO buffer at O0.
+        //
+        // That combination trips a fatal error in stage0 compilers linked against
+        // LLVM 23 that predate the `AssignGUIDPass` fix ("expected function
+        // definition <name> to have an associated value info"). Nothing links
+        // host build artifacts with LTO, so just restore Cargo's own default here
+        // -- `RUSTC_HOST_FLAGS` is appended after Cargo's arguments, so this wins.
+        hostflags.arg("-Cembed-bitcode=no");
+
         // `rustc` needs to know the remapping scheme, in order to know how to reverse it (unremap)
         // later. Two env vars are set and made available to the compiler
